# Hello, world on every board: the program writes "Hello, world!" over the serial output of the board (the console of
# Asmonite on it: the tab Serial shows it). The same source for the ESP32, the ESP32-S3, the ESP32-C3, the ESP32-S31,
# the Raspberry Pi Pico and the Pico 2 (also with WiFi): it has no line target "...", so Asmonite translates it for the
# board of Project > aBelle for (the board in the tab Serial), and include "console.abel" takes the functions of the
# console of that board from abelle\lib. Start it with F9.
include "console.abel"

def main():
    println("Hello, world!")
